-- title:
--   Degree of level N₀ℓ q over level N₀q under q↦ q^ℓ
-- statement:
--   Fix natural numbers $N_0$, $q$, $\ell$ with $N_0 \neq 0$ and with $q$ and $\ell$ prime, and assume $\ell \neq q$. For a natural number $N \neq 0$ write $F_N = \mathbb{Q}\bigl(\,\mathrm{qExpand}_d(j_q) : d \mid N,\ d \neq 0\,\bigr)$ for the intermediate field `modularFunctionFieldFull N` of $\mathbb{Q} \subseteq \mathbb{Q}(\!(q)\!)$ generated by the Laurent series obtained from the $q$-expansion $j_q$ by the substitutions $q \mapsto q^{d}$ over the nonzero divisors $d$ of $N$; here $\mathrm{qExpand}_d$ is the ring endomorphism of $\mathbb{Q}(\!(q)\!)$ that multiplies all exponents by $d$. Let $\varphi \colon F_{N_0 q} \to F_{N_0 \ell q}$ be a ring homomorphism which on underlying Laurent series is the substitution $q \mapsto q^{\ell}$, i.e. the image of each $f \in F_{N_0q}$ under $\varphi$ has Laurent series $\mathrm{qExpand}_\ell$ applied to that of $f$. Then $F_{N_0\ell q}$, viewed as a module over $F_{N_0q}$ through the algebra structure induced by $\varphi$, has finite rank equal to $\ell$ if $\ell \mid N_0$, and to $\ell + 1$ otherwise.
--
--   Classically this is the degree of the degeneracy map on function fields corresponding to the index $[\Gamma_0(N_0q) : \Gamma_0(N_0\ell q)] = \psi(N_0\ell q)/\psi(N_0 q)$, in the shape needed when a fixed auxiliary prime $q$ is already present in the level and a new prime $\ell$ is added. It feeds the flatness and rank computation for the Hecke degeneracy curve change, [`ModularCurve.DRModelPackageLevel.isFinite_flat_finrank_curveChange_heckeDegeneracy_rat`](thm.html#ModularCurve.DRModelPackageLevel.isFinite_flat_finrank_curveChange_heckeDegeneracy_rat).
